Package: meetinginsights
Version: 0.1.1
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-venv, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-webkit2-4.0, gir1.2-notify-0.7, pulseaudio-utils, ffmpeg, curl, libc6 (>= 2.14), libgcc-s1, libstdc++6
Installed-Size: 43764
Maintainer: techbysaurabh <hi.techbysaurabh@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/techbysaurabh/meetinginsights-linux
Description: On-device meeting recorder and AI note taker
 MeetingInsights records a meeting from the microphone and system audio,
 transcribes it locally with faster-whisper and writes structured minutes
 with a small local language model. No account, no API key, and no audio
 ever leaves the machine.
 .
 Speaker attribution comes from audio routing rather than a diarization
 model: the microphone is recorded to the left channel and system audio to
 the right, so action-item owners are read off the transcript instead of
 being inferred.
 .
 A one-time "meetinginsights setup" downloads the speech and language
 models (about 1.5 GB) and prepares the Python environment.
